        <p>_ Breakfast was served at 7.30, and then Sergeant Goodwin instructed them in the rudiments of judging distance and elementary observation. Before leaving the farm at two o'clock, Sergeant Goodwin thanked Squire Withington and Mr. Lawton for their generosity. The lads supported with three hearty cheers. Squire Withington extended a further invitation to the lads on any future occasion.</p>
