      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-07-01_WidnesExaminer_art0120" n="art0120">
        <head>SOUTH LANCS. WIN TUG-OF-WAR ON THE EAST COAST.</head>
        <p>SOUTH LANCS. WIN TUG-OF-WAR ON THE EAST COAST.</p>
        <p>On Wednesday afternoon a very interesting athletic festival was held somewhere on the East Coast in connection with the A.S.C. The crew of No. 2. Armoured Train furnished the winning team in the open tug of war, defeat- ing the Heavy Battery R.G.A., Provisional Battalion and the R.F.A., each by two pulls to none.</p>
        <p>The victorious team consisted of Lance- Corporals Woodward and Roughley, Privates. Smith, Glynn, Berks, Stokes (all of the South Lancashire Territorials) and Gunners Levitt and Heod--(Bussex.R.G.A.). . _</p>
