        <p>THE following is a List of the Names of Men who have failed to present themselves at WARRINGTON, after being called up either under the Group System or the Military Service Act, 1916.</p>
        <p>Anyone who can give information regarding any of the above-named absentees is invited to do 80, either personally or by letter, to the nearest Recruiting Officer. The names of individuals giving such information will on no account be disclosed. D. T. MOCATTA, Lt.-Colonel, RECRUITING OFFICER. 1 IF ERRORS OCCUR. Lieutenant-Colonel Mocatta, Recruiting Officer, Warrington, has informed us that the list published to-day of men who have failed to present themselves after being called up is issued on War Office Instructions. He tells us that it has been compiled with the utmost care, but points out that it is possible that names may appear in the list of men who have died or have enlisted in another Area, or have been prevented by severe illness or other legitimate cause from reporting themselves. .If this should happen in isolated cases, Colonel Mocatta desires to express his regret, but at the same time to point out that it is almost impossible to deal with thousands of names without one or two errors of this kind.—ED. "EXAMINER.''</p>
