        <p>POLITICS IN COURT. Smart "Retort "By "Pipe Jumper" At Gas Works. What is a pipe jumper? The question was answered at the Munitions Court on Monday afternoon. The phrase suggests some kind of acrobatic performance, but it really identifies a pipe cleaner in a gas works. John Dolan, employed in this capacity at :he local gas works, alleged that a certificate for which he had applied was wrongfully ,withheld by the fitm on June 20th. He explained that he had been engaged at pipe-jumping," other- wise pipe cleaning, and was earning on an average £2 2s. weekly. He was transferred to ' work in the yard, where his pay was reduced to 295. lid., and another man named McGrath was put to his former job. He Considered this unfair, and also complained that he ,had been deprived of a Sunday shift, which carried double pay. - , Mr. Arthur Yates, assistant engineer at the gas works, said it was only recently that Dolan was doing the work of pipe jumping. During the majority of his time in the works he was employed filling fires, and his pay was 375. Ed His exact pay was 375. 6d., and his present wages 30s. 3d. Dolan interjected that 4d. was taken off. Mr. Yates: Yes, for insurance. Dolan: Well, I don't get it. (Laughter.) Mr. Yates added that Dolan shared" the :Is. bonus for married men. McGrath was an older hand than Dolan. It was further er•plained that the latter was taken off owing to the de- crease in the use of gas—much smaller than that in winter time—and to the fact that some of the retorts were not needed. Dolan was understood to ask Mr. Yates what would happen when more men were required. Mr. Yates: We must wait and see. Dolan: That is what Asquith said. The certificate was granted. A Country Solomon. Two brothers inherited a farm and quarrelled violently as to its division. Now there lived in their village a certain shrewd and wise old man, noted for the sound- ness of his advice. Him the brothers deter- mined to appoint arbitrator. Whatever he ' said they would ,abide by. They laid the matter before him. For, a long while he thought, then delivered judgment. "You," he said, pointing to the elder, "shall divide the farm as you think fair. And yon," he continued, pointing to the younger, "shall have the first choice."</p>
